WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.870
The "Conjuring" series of movies has been
going for a full decade now, and it's been

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.490
a runaway success since pretty much the start.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.980
But what about quality?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.879
Which of the eight movies are blessed, and
which ones are demonically bad?

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:19.539
The 2014 "Conjuring" prequel "Annabelle" made
a respectable $257 million worldwide, but

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:22.282
reactions to the film were far from kind.

00:00:22.282 --> 00:00:26.619
One look at the movie's Rotten Tomatoes scores
shows that filmgoers and critics alike weren't

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:29.007
pleased with the possessed doll's antics.

00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:33.010
Based on the Annabelle doll first seen in
"The Conjuring," this spin-off focuses on

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.480
a couple welcoming their first child.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.550
The doll terrorizes these new parents and
seems intent on taking their daughter's soul,

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.270
but it turns out that it's the mom's soul
the demon is after.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.390
What sets "Annabelle" apart from other entries
in the Conjuring Universe is just how stale

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.077
and uneventful the overall film feels.

00:00:50.077 --> 00:00:54.210
Outside of some shots of the doll looking
intimidating or being positioned ominously

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.720
in a room, there isn't really much to keep
audiences on the edge of their seats.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.587
"That doll.

00:01:00.587 --> 00:01:04.750
We have to get rid of it."

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:09.480
Not only is the film's antagonist a bore,
the human characters also lack personality.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.259
Plus, the ending, in which the movie's only
Black character sacrifices herself to save

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:17.490
the white protagonist, led to some serious
criticism.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.460
The concept of a killer doll isn't exactly
new, and with so many better entries into

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.070
the genre to choose from, "Annabelle" is completely
forgettable.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:29.110
Also, just to note: Despite the priest from
"Annabelle" appearing in "The Curse of La

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:33.820
Llorona," the latter movie's director clarified
that it isn't actually part of the "Conjuring"

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.407
series, so it isn't on our list.

00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:41.290
"The Nun" boasts some haunting, Gothic set
design and striking period costumes.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:45.310
The film might be the most visually interesting
entry in the "Conjuring" franchise.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:49.430
However, some pretty production design isn't
enough to make a film function, and it's safe

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.797
to say viewers weren't impressed with this
entry overall.

00:01:52.797 --> 00:01:57.027
It's set in 1952, and features a group of
nuns living in a Romanian abbey.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.700
They discover that World War II bombs have
reopened a spiritual rift that once was sealed

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.590
to keep demons from entering into the world.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:08.509
The film follows a novitiate who is determined
to find the root of the evil emanating from

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.382
the monastery and banish a spirit called Valak
that has taken the form of an undead nun.

00:02:13.382 --> 00:02:18.250
In the end, the movie looks nice, but is packed
with one-note characters, lazy dialogue, and

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:23.010
forgettable jump scares, "The Nun" manages
to feel completely flat and devoid of creative

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.560
substance, despite having some stylistic flair.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:30.730
"The Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It" follows
paranormal investigators Ed and Lorraine Warren

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.700
as they try to save a young man named Arne,
who accidentally invited a demon into his

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.550
body during an exorcism on his younger brother.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:43.355
"Whatever happened that day, that was not
Arne."

00:02:43.355 --> 00:02:48.409
Set in 1981, the third "Conjuring" movie takes
the Warrens on a convoluted journey that involves

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:51.580
dangerous totems and a curse rooted in the
occult.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.310
In their efforts to help Arne, the Warrens
learn that there is much more lurking beneath

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.890
the surface of this possession.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:02.209
They also help make history by supporting
Arne in a landmark trial after he kills his landlord.

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.090
This element of the story is based on the
real-life murder trial of Arne Johnson, in

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.819
which the Warrens were involved.

00:03:08.432 --> 00:03:12.617
"I think it's about time they accept the existence
of the devil."

00:03:12.967 --> 00:03:17.930
While "The Devil Made Me Do It" isn't the
worst movie in the franchise, it also isn't the best.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.920
It ups the ante, particularly for Lorraine,
but it relies too heavily on tired jump scares.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.530
The demon is one of the least impactful in
the series as well.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.280
If you thought you'd seen the last of Valak,
you were wrong.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.430
"The Nun II" picks up four years after the
events of the first "Nun," following Sister

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.569
Irene in Italy.

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:38.030
She now leads a simpler life after her last
encounter with the demon.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.620
However, that peace is interrupted when she's
asked to investigate some unusual deaths taking

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.269
place across the continent.

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:52.099
"I think there's something here that's not
meant to be."

00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:56.380
What follows is a story that gives more insight
into the demon that includes missing eyes,

00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:00.640
killing the descendants of the saint that
took them, and a delivery boy-turned-puppet.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.660
As Sister Irene dives further into history
in her attempts to send Valak back to Hell

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.420
for good, she also learns more about her own
ancestry and the power of a mother's love.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.450
"The Nun II" is a sequel that improves on
the mistakes of its predecessor.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:18.100
Valak is given real motives this time around,
rather than just being a scary presence, and

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.989
one of the other nuns is given a subplot that's
actually culturally relevant.

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:25.560
While the movie is ultimately an improvement
over the first, and is better than recent

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.320
films in the universe, it's still a middle-of-the-road
entry.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.370
In this third "Annabelle" film, Ed and Lorraine
Warren come into possession of the cursed

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:38.112
Annabelle doll, the couple safely lock the
possessed plaything away in their occult museum.

00:04:38.112 --> 00:04:43.012
Protected by a glass case and shielded from
the outside world, it looks like all is well.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:46.567
"It's safer for these things to be in here
than out there.

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:49.407
Sometimes it's better to keep the genie in
the bottle."

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.690
Of course, one slip up is all it takes for
Annabelle to cause havoc.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.900
When the Warrens' daughter Judy is left in
the care of teenage babysitter Mary Ellen,

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.500
the haunted doll seizes on the opportunity.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:04.780
Shortly after Mary Ellen arrives, her friend
Daniela makes an unplanned visit.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.071
Daniela is hoping to reconnect with her deceased
father, so she trespasses into the Warrens'

00:05:09.071 --> 00:05:12.560
locked artifact room and accidentally releases
Annabelle.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.670
A "beacon for other spirits," Annabelle sets
free a slew of spooky entities from the couple's

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:23.520
collection of cursed objects, turning the
once peaceful Warren home into a demonic house of horrors.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:27.620
You would think a cast of wacky demons running
wild would result in some creative scares,

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.865
and there are a few.

00:05:28.865 --> 00:05:33.035
But most of the film is just a slow build-up
for one jump scare after another.

00:05:33.035 --> 00:05:37.080
None of the demons really get enough focus
to make them stand out from the more interesting

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.310
cast of unholy spirits from previous films.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:45.090
"The Conjuring 2" is one of the best received
entries in the series, but it nonetheless

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.600
feels a little like the creative team tried
and failed to recapture lightning in a bottle

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.100
with this sequel.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.360
In the end, "The Conjuring 2" feels like it
was made with the intention of setting up

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.630
an expanded universe instead of telling a
complete, self-contained story, especially

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.860
considering the spin-offs that followed soon
afterward.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.810
Aside from the crowded roster of spirits,
the primary demon gives its name to Lorraine

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:09.247
in the beginning of the movie, which is the
key to defeating it in the end.

00:06:09.247 --> 00:06:12.957
It makes the resolution feel not only rushed,
but unearned.

00:06:12.957 --> 00:06:17.000
Despite these gripes, "The Conjuring 2" is
still a worthy successor to the first film,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.930
making use of interesting camera work, slow
build-ups, and the sort of creepy imagery

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.400
that fans of the franchise have come to expect.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:28.744
A prequel to the first "Annabelle" film, "Annabelle:
Creation" shows the origin of the demonic doll.

00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:32.449
The film opens with a couple witnessing the
death of their young daughter, Annabelle,

00:06:32.449 --> 00:06:34.070
nicknamed "Bee."

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.280
The grieving parents are willing to make any
bargain just to spend more time with her,

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.950
and when a spirit begins making itself known
in their house, they think they may have gotten their wish.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:47.010
But Bee isn't the same upon her return, and
they soon realize that they've invited a demon

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.949
to reside in their daughter's doll.

00:06:48.949 --> 00:06:56.410
"So we locked it away, where it could be surrounded
by the word of God."

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:01.122
To repent for their actions, the couple takes
in a group of girls from a recently closed orphanage.

00:07:01.122 --> 00:07:04.471
Unfortunately for them, Annabelle wants to
play.

00:07:04.629 --> 00:07:08.180
The cast of child actors does a good job,
and there's some decent writing to support

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.300
them as well.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:12.979
There are some genuinely terrifying visuals
that help drive home the sadistic nature of

00:07:12.979 --> 00:07:13.979
the demon.

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:18.100
There is a unique balance in "Annabelle: Creation"
between highlighting the emotional punishment

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:22.379
endured by the people in the house and the
physical punishment doled out by the sadistic

00:07:22.379 --> 00:07:26.792
spirit, letting the two complement each other
and build in anxiety-inducing ways.

00:07:26.792 --> 00:07:28.202
"What are you guys?"

00:07:28.202 --> 00:07:30.540
"Well we've been called ghost hunters, paranormal
researchers"

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:34.275
"But we prefer to be known simply as Ed and
Lorraine Warren"

00:07:34.275 --> 00:07:39.160
Critics and fans agree: the first entry in
the franchise is also the best.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.910
Instead of being thrown into the paranormal
with little explanation, the characters are

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:47.659
forced to do research, set up and monitor
equipment, and work with local police just

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:50.650
to get enough proof to have an exorcism approved.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:54.800
As a result of all the added legwork, not
only does "The Conjuring" feel more believable

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:59.039
and accessible for audiences, but the frightening
payoffs feel earned.

00:07:59.039 --> 00:08:02.336
The chief marker of this film's quality is
the building of atmosphere.

00:08:02.336 --> 00:08:07.712
This is demonstrated particularly well through
how reserved and understated some of the scares are.

00:08:07.712 --> 00:08:11.660
The musical score is allowed to be soft and
to serve as a background to scares, instead

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.820
of the blaring, bass-heavy blasts in later
movies.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.960
The minimal CGI used throughout the film is
also done with precision, demonstrating the

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:23.023
common adage — particularly true in horror
— that less is more.

